## Judge scheme (mt_foreign_free_probe)
# Owner thread allocates N blocks (locality: classes 16/64/256, <=4 segment
# bases; capacity: 256B class across >4 segment bases, frees interleaved
# across bases). Worker warms its OWN heap pre-window (own alloc/free x128) so
# current_for_dealloc = Own and dealloc_routing's owned_block_of/hash_find
# miss is actually exercised. Measured window: worker ONLY calls
# #[inline(never)] w_free (GlobalAlloc::dealloc). Owner drains after join
# (trim_current_thread). Own control mode: worker pre-allocates its OWN blocks
# pre-window; window frees only those. Oracle (separate bench-internals
# build): SeferAlloc::dbg_b4_collapse_counters()[3]=B4_FOREIGN_PUBLISH_OK,
# [4]=B4_DIRECTORY_LOOKUPS; RoutePin::dbg_route_pin_cache_totals() hits/misses.

